        "original_id": "50acf928-e7ef-5b84-82e2-772a5c6d83d5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Beyazıt Tower, Beyazıt Square, Istanbul, Turkey, Golden Horn, Fatih district\n- Organizations: Istanbul University, Ottoman Ministry of War\n- Products: Miniatürk\n- Systems: Istanbul University Observatory\n- Concepts: Seraskier Tower, Forum Tauri, seven hills of Istanbul\n- People: Constantine the Great\n\nFacts:\n- Beyazıt Square in Istanbul, Turkey, was known as the Forum Tauri in the Roman period.\n- Constantine the Great built Istanbul following the model of Rome on seven hills.\n- In 1936, Istanbul University Observatory was established next to Beyazıt Tower within Istanbul University's main campus at Beyazıt Square in Fatih district, Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Beyazıt Tower, also named Seraskier Tower after the Ottoman Ministry of War, is an 85 m tall fire-watch tower in the courtyard of Istanbul University's main campus on Beyazıt Square in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Istanbul University's main campus was formerly the Ottoman Ministry of War.\n- Miniatürk is a miniature park on the north-eastern shore of the Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
